=====================================
START PROGRAM
=====================================

    Create the 40-space Monopoly board
    Initialize the player position at GO (position 0)

    Set total moves to 0
    Set landing counter for every square to 0

    Create Chance deck
    Create Community Chest deck

    Shuffle both decks

    Initialize Get Out of Jail Free card tracking

END INITIALIZATION

-------------------------------------
FUNCTION rollDice()
-------------------------------------

    Roll first six-sided die
    Roll second six-sided die

    RETURN sum of both dice

END FUNCTION

-------------------------------------
FUNCTION movePlayer(steps)
-------------------------------------

    Update player position by adding steps

    IF position is greater than 39
        Wrap around to GO
    END IF

    RETURN new position

END FUNCTION

-------------------------------------
FUNCTION resolveSpace()
-------------------------------------

    CHECK current board position

    IF space is Chance
        Draw Chance card
        Apply card effect

    ELSE IF space is Community Chest
        Draw Community Chest card
        Apply card effect

    ELSE IF space is Go To Jail
        Send player to Jail

    ELSE
        Keep player on current square
    END IF

    IF a card moves the player
        Resolve the destination space if required
    END IF

    RETURN final player position

END FUNCTION

-------------------------------------
FUNCTION takeTurn(strategy)
-------------------------------------

    Set consecutive doubles to 0

    WHILE player has not completed turn

        Roll two dice

        IF both dice are equal
            Increase consecutive doubles
        ELSE
            Reset consecutive doubles if appropriate
        END IF

        IF consecutive doubles equals 3
            Send player to Jail
            END TURN
        END IF

        Move player forward

        Resolve current board space

        IF player is sent to Jail
            END TURN
        END IF

        IF dice are not doubles
            END TURN
        END IF

    END WHILE

    Increase total moves

    Increase landing counter for final square

END FUNCTION

-------------------------------------
FUNCTION jailStrategyA()
-------------------------------------

    IF player has Get Out of Jail Free card
        Use card
        Return player to normal play

    ELSE
        Assume player pays $50
        Release player immediately
        Return player to normal play
    END IF

END FUNCTION

-------------------------------------
FUNCTION jailStrategyB()
-------------------------------------

    IF player has Get Out of Jail Free card
        Use card
        Return player to normal play

    ELSE
        Attempt to roll doubles for up to 3 turns

        IF doubles are rolled
            Release player
            Move according to dice
        ELSE
            After 3 unsuccessful attempts
                Assume player pays $50
                Release player on 4th turn
        END IF
    END IF

END FUNCTION

-------------------------------------
FUNCTION runSimulation(strategy, numberOfTurns)
-------------------------------------

    Reset player position to GO
    Reset landing counters
    Reset player and deck state

    FOR turn = 1 TO numberOfTurns

        IF player is in Jail
            Apply selected jail strategy
        ELSE
            takeTurn(strategy)
        END IF

    END FOR

    FOR each square on the board

        Calculate landing percentage:

        percentage = (landing count / numberOfTurns) * 100

        Output square name
        Output landing count
        Output landing percentage

    END FOR

END FUNCTION

=====================================
MAIN PROGRAM
=====================================

    Set turn counts:
        1,000
        10,000
        100,000
        1,000,000

    FOR each jail strategy (A and B)

        FOR simulation = 1 TO 10

            FOR each turn count

                Run simulation using selected strategy

                Save landing counts
                Save landing percentages

            END FOR

        END FOR

    END FOR

    Generate comparison summary

    Identify top 3–5 most-landed-on squares

    Compare Strategy A and Strategy B

    Check whether results stabilize as turns increase

    Output final results

END PROGRAM

-------------------------------------
FUNCTION compareResults()
-------------------------------------

    Display top 5 squares for Strategy A
    Display top 5 squares for Strategy B

    Compare landing percentages at 1,000,000 turns

    Identify squares with the largest differences

    Determine whether both strategies approach
    similar landing probability distributions

    Identify unexpected results or anomalies

END FUNCTION